+# The Daily Grind
+
+Responsive homepage and rewards registration with email ownership verification through Google Identity Services. No OTP or magic-link email is sent.
+
+## Configuration
+
+Requires Node.js 22.13+ (Node 24 recommended) and pnpm. Install with `pnpm install`. Set `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` to a Google OAuth **Web application** client ID and `PUBLIC_ORIGIN` to the exact public origin (scheme, hostname, and port). Add that same origin to the client's **Authorized JavaScript origins** in Google Cloud Console. No client secret is required. `.env.example` documents the variables; the server reads process environment variables, so load them through your deployment environment or Node's `--env-file` option.
+
+`pnpm build` checks JavaScript syntax without starting a server. `pnpm start` runs the Node server, serving both the homepage and API on `PORT` (default 11222). Production requires an HTTPS `PUBLIC_ORIGIN`, `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`, and `NODE_ENV=production`. The original static server cannot provide the verification API.
+
+Without a configured client ID, the homepage is fully viewable and sign-up displays an honest availability message. No simulated verification or account creation is used. Real sign-in requires the configured Google application and network access to Google. Gmail and Google Workspace mailboxes are supported. Third-party email addresses attached to a Google account are rejected because Google cannot attest to their current mailbox ownership.
+
+## Registration flow
+
+1. The form collects name, email, required terms acceptance, and optional marketing consent.
+2. `POST /api/rewards/challenge` takes `{email}` and creates a ten-minute session with a cryptographic nonce in a server-only map. A same-site, HttpOnly cookie binds it to the browser; HTTPS adds Secure and the `__Host-` prefix.
+3. Google Identity Services confirms the selected Google identity in a popup/browser identity UI. No inbox access is requested.
+4. `POST /api/rewards/verify-email` takes `{email, credential}`. The server verifies Google's RS256 signature against its rotating keys, issuer, audience, authorized party, token age and expiry, session nonce, exact normalized email, verified-email claim, and authoritative email provider. It consumes the nonce before asynchronous verification. Only the server records verified status.
+5. `POST /api/rewards/register` takes `{firstName, lastName, email, terms: true, marketing: boolean}`. It requires the verified session, stores membership, and consumes the session. Duplicate emails and Google identities are rejected. Direct registration without proof is denied.
+
+All POSTs require the configured Origin and JSON. Bodies and request times are bounded. API responses disable caching, inputs are checked on the server, registration requests are rate limited, and static serving uses an explicit allowlist. Tokens are not persisted or logged. Session expiration, wrong email/account, denied verification, loading/network failures, and duplicate membership produce visible messages.
+
+## Storage and deployment
+
+SQLite persists rewards members under `data/rewards.sqlite`, or in `DATA_DIR` when configured. Mount a persistent private volume and restrict access to it. The database records zero initial points and an available welcome drink. Redemption, purchase integration, marketing delivery, birthday collection, and ongoing account sign-in are outside this registration implementation; connect café operations before offering live redemption.
+
+Registration sessions and rate limits are in memory, intended for a single Node instance. Restarting the process expires pending registrations. Use shared session/rate-limit storage before deploying multiple instances. Behind a proxy, the current socket-address limiter may group visitors; configure a trusted proxy layer with its own limits. Do not expose the database or environment files through a separate static server. Review the included program terms and privacy copy against actual café operations before launch.
+
+Verification reference: https://developers.google.com/identity/gsi/web/guides/verify-google-id-token
+
+No development/preview server was started and no manual browser verification was performed during implementation.
